# No ship without OK (always on)

Applies to **all** Mode A / outward work: packs, HTML, Excel, zip, Outlook to colleagues, dashboards — not IDS-only. Overrides “helpful” drive-bys. **Banned phrase:** “fix if safe.” Do not invent waivers.

## 1. Mail — draft by default; Send only on explicit current ask

- Outlook / email / `.msg` / Copilot: **Draft + Display** by default.
- **Send** only when the **current** message explicitly says **send** / **verstuur** / clear equivalent for **that** mail.
- Forbidden: Send because “he said send earlier”, urgency, or agent convenience.
- After any Send (or when he says he sent): run the **mail delivery loop** — prove **Sent Items** (subject + To + attachments) or report **Outbox stuck**. Never claim delivered without that proof.
- Full procedure: skill `isze-mail-delivery` + rule `isze-mail-delivery-loop.mdc`.

## 2. Versions — no silent overwrite

- Any **versioned** deliverable (v1.3, deck rev, pack label, filename version): if **content** changes, **stop and ask** — new version label (e.g. v1.4) or leave as-is?
- **Forbidden:** rebuild under the same label and claim it is still the old version.
- Do not invent or bump version labels without his OK.

## 3. Rebuild / ship — explicit words only

- **Default MODE = SPAR** — see `isze-spar-default.mdc`. Remarks and attached plans are not go.
- Default for packs, HTML, Excel, zips, Mode A outputs: **read-only**.
- Write / regenerate / ship / sync-as-deliverable **only** when the **current** message explicitly says **rebuild** or **ship** (or clear equivalent he uses the same way).
- “Implement the plan” alone is **not** enough if purpose is still open or he is sparring — require **rebuild**/**ship** in that message.
- Check / investigate / QA = **read only**. No “while I’m here” mutation of client files.
- Ask before expanding scope (extra countries, extra recipients, INDEX/manifest bumps).
- Do **not** ship a **new** HTML filename under `02_dashboards/`. Change the existing file for that home.

## 4. Known-bad metrics — don’t touch until asked

- If a number/average/score is known broken or flagged in chat/memory: **leave it**. Note it if useful; do **not** quietly fix, recompute into deliverables, or “correct” averages without an explicit ask.
- Same for any pending decision metric — awareness ≠ permission to patch.

**IDS QA after authorized rebuild:** `isze-ids-delivery.mdc` (tiles/geo/UI) — that file is not permission to rebuild.
